{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Two male lambs and one ewe lamb.</b> Because the affliction of tzara'at is a consequence of the act of the tongue, therefore he offers one lamb as a burnt offering, like the rule of every burnt offering, on account of the spirit; and one as a guilt offering, like the rule of every guilt offering; and a female as a sin offering, like the rule of every sin offering; and three tenths, like the rule of a tenth per lamb." "<b>And one log.</b> A measure that has no brother. The meaning of those lambs and the ewe, likewise this guilt offering, likewise this sin offering, is for the priest, apart from those mentioned."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:06.053121293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}